    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="0234" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg114"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chinese
                    Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 54.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note No. 50, of the 4th instant, calling attention to the drowning of Ho
                    Choy Yeen, a Chinese subject, at Canton, China, by certain sailors from an
                    American war vessel on September 26 last, and expressing the hope that such
                    action in the matter will be taken by this government as will satisfy the
                    demands of justice.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform you that the matter will be given immediate
                    attention.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. B. Loomis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
